WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.036
-Welcome back, everybody.
I'm here with Questlove, Tariq,

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.938
Kirk, Mark, and Dave
from The Roots.

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:07.640
And we're at Luna Park
in Coney Island, Brooklyn.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.242
People have been coming here
for over 100 years to have fun,

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:12.846
go on rides, play games,
and be entertained.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.280
There's an energy to this place,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.816
a spirit, a magic.
And with that in mind,

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.619
I invited Justin Willman
to show us a new trick.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.786
I think he's right this way.

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:22.388
Let's check it out.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:28.561 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:34.700 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.569
-What's up?
-What's up, bud? How you doing?

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.104
-Good to see you. I'm good.
It's great to see you.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.138
Hi, guys.
-Hey, what's up?

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:40.673
-What's up, man?
-Welcome to Coney Island.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:41.807
-Wow.
-Thanks.

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:42.909
-Since we're in
Coney Island, Brooklyn,

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.844
I thought we'd play
a game tonight.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.646
-Okay.
-Okay? Now, this is a game

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.481
that my dad used to play with me
when I was a kid.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.949
My dad's not a magician.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.518
My dad was an airline pilot
for TWA back in the day.

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:53.919
Remember TWA?
-Of course.

00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:56.155
-Quality airline.
So, he'd come home from a trip,

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:57.490
and we'd have
a family game night.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.926
And we'd always play
this one game that he invented

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.494
called Right on the Money.
-Okay.

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:02.695
-Alright?
Here's how it went down.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.830
He took a handful of coins
out of his pocket.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:07.299
He poured them into
this little cigar humidor box

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:08.667
so I couldn't count them.

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.536
On the wall,
he had a map of the U.S.,

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.905
and all the 50 states
had a different point value.

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:14.073
You follow?
-Yeah.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.541
-He'd give me some darts.

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:18.144
I'd throw the darts at the map
till I hit four states.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.480
I'd total up the score of the
states with an old calculator,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.782
and if my score equaled the
amount of change in the box --

00:01:23.782 --> 00:01:25.418
150 points, $1.50 in the box --

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.820
it meant I'd won.
I was right on the money.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.956
And as a prize,
my dad would take me on a trip

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.557
anywhere in the world
I wanted to go.

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:33.058
-Wow.
-Wow.

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:36.029
-And over the years, my dad and
I went on zero trips together.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.396
[ Laughter ]
-I was gonna say.

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:39.565
-'Cause this game sucked.
And I forgot about the game

00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:42.335
until my son Jackson's 2nd
birthday earlier this year.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.671
My dad, in a very sweet gesture,

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:48.140
gifted us his cigar humidor

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.176
with the darts

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.544
and the old calculator.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:54.647
Even made a brand-new map
of the U.S.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.215
And I'd be honored, Jimmy,

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:57.983
if you would play
the role of my son.

00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.251
-[ Laughs ]
-Aww.

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:00.653
-Perfect.
-They grow up so fast.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:03.056
This is perfect. Okay. Now,
and this is what's exciting.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:05.458
So, NBC's arranged
a great prize.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:08.160
If you win, Jimmy,
if you're right on the money,

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.795
